# Allow-list: git tracks code, docs and small derived tables only.
# Raw data (logs, per-trial key-value files, archives) is published as GitHub Release
# assets, with checksums in DATA.md. See docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md.

# Ignore everything...
*
# ...but descend into directories,
!*/

# and track these.
!.gitignore
!Makefile
# code
!*.c
!*.h
!*.cu
!*.cc
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.diff
# docs
!*.md
# derived tables, experiment specs and small text records
!*.csv
!*.txt
!*.json
!*.spec

# Never track these, even if they match the allow-list above.
__pycache__/
# Claude Code: only the root project skills are shared; worktrees, local state and any
# nested .claude folders stay out.
**/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
**/build/
**/install/

# Inside result folders only the tables (*.csv) and write-ups (*.md) are tracked;
# everything else there is raw data and goes to the release assets.
**/results/**/*.txt
**/results/**/*.json
**/results/**/*.spec

# Session QA notes stay local.
harness/QA_20260923.md
